From 2dc3e1992e0080a8de4fc86a236f7c2b6dc3d56e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:31:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: Give Madai CPR an independent MX sleep guard

Name a separate L3 sleep-only voter for the experimental CPU target. CPR
retains its supported maximum while APC remains live, independently of
ACTIVE scaling and Pronto's persistent normal sleep settings. The RPM
provider retains independent boot holds and rearms the SLEEP hold when
the CPU sleep consumer is released after a failed probe.

This depends on the independent SO provider and optional CPR sleep guard.
It does not lower the sleep request to the binding minimum, add full
CPU/L2/RPM/MPM entry, or remove the existing CPR deep-suspend guard.
The ordinary board and all other hardware targets are unchanged.

Codex generated this change and its host qualification. Human review and
DCO certification remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.

Backport this prerequisite to maintained Linux 6.18.63. The complete
seventeen-change batch passes native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT object
builds with the MSM8926 feature enabled and disabled. CPU-idle is ARM
only. Host fault models use synthetic services and normal LeakSanitizer;
firmware, electrical and physical suspend acceptance remain open.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Original authors,
dates, licenses and human attribution tags are retained. Human DCO and
review remain pending. No phone access or publication occurred.

Backported from commit ca964cab8969 ("ARM: dts: qcom: Give Madai CPR
an independent MX sleep guard")
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
index 96fc912b7dfb3..92340f2bf2f84 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
@@ -215,6 +215,7 @@ cpr: power-controller@f9018000 {
 		qcom,apcs-syscon = <&apcs>;
 		vdd-apc-supply = <&pm8226_apc>;
 		vdd-mx-supply = <&pm8226_l3_ao>;
+		vdd-mx-sleep-supply = <&pm8226_l3_so>;
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		operating-points-v2 = <&cpr_opp_table>;
 		nvmem-cells = <&cpu_speedbin>, <&cpr_primary>, <&cpr_redundant>;
@@ -230,5 +231,10 @@ pm8226_l3_ao: l3-ao {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <750000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1337500>;
 		};
+
+		pm8226_l3_so: l3-so {
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <750000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1337500>;
+		};
 	};
 };
